course: dictionary
lesson: 4190
title: Saying goodbye
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Goodbye is what you say when you leave someone, or when they leave you. «Goodbye, and thank you for having me» is a polite way to end a visit to a friend's house.
explain: Goodbye can also be a noun, meaning the act of saying it. In «a sad goodbye», the word names the moment of parting itself. Writers use this to show feelings, such as moving away or losing a pet.
explain: Look at the words around goodbye to find its tone. «Moving means packing everything, doing paperwork and saying goodbye all at once, so it is very stressful.» The clue is stressful, so saying goodbye here is a hard, tiring part of moving.
fact: Goodbye is what you say when you leave someone, or when they leave you.
fact: A goodbye is the act of saying goodbye, as in «a sad goodbye».
fact: Shorter, casual goodbyes include bye, see you, see you later and catch you later.
fact: Other places have their own goodbyes: cheerio (UK), see ya or hooroo (Australia), and «na vsE DObre», which means take care.
fact: Good-bye and good-by are other spellings; good-by is used in the USA.
exercise: What is goodbye used for? | *Saying it when you leave someone, or when they leave you | Asking someone where they live | Saying hello at the start of a visit
exercise: In «a sad goodbye», what is goodbye? | *The act of saying goodbye | A question | A place to stay | A shop
exercise: Which goodbye is short and casual? | Pleased to meet you | Yours sincerely | *See you later | Good evening
test: «Moving means packing everything and saying goodbye all at once, so it is very stressful.» What does saying goodbye suggest here? | Something happy and quick | A game for the children | Shopping for food | *A hard, tiring part of moving
test: Which goodbye is used in Australia? | Good morning | Thank you very much | *Hooroo | Pleased to meet you
exam: Which sentence uses goodbye as a noun? | Goodbye, friend, come again | *She gave a sad goodbye at the station | Goodbye, see you tomorrow!
